# Build output — builds are ALWAYS out-of-tree via $env:LUAUG_BUILD_ROOT (rule R14).
# These patterns are defensive only; nothing should ever create them in-tree.
#
# ROOT-ANCHORED, and that leading slash is load-bearing. Unanchored, `build-*/`
# matches at any depth, which silently swallowed
# third_party/sdl_shadercross/build-scripts/ — upstream source, including the
# very file ADR 0032 cites — on the way into the repo. A vendored tree is
# upstream's tracked files by construction (ADR 0021); our own ignore rules have
# no business deciding which of them survive.
/build/
/build-*/
/out/
/cmake-build-*/
/.cache/

# Local tooling installed by scripts/bootstrap (Lute binary etc.)
.tooling/

# Generated per-project state of example/user projects
.luaug/

# Bytecode / shader / asset caches
*.luauc
shaders/compiled/
content/cache/

# Gradle's own state for the Android package. Root-anchored patterns above
# cannot reach it, and Android Studio creates both on first open.
/samples/triangle/android/.gradle/
/samples/triangle/android/local.properties

# IDE / editor cruft
.vs/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.swp
*~

# OS / sync artifacts
desktop.ini
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
~$*

# Logs, dumps, profiling traces
*.log
*.dmp
*.perfetto-trace

# Packaging output
dist/
*.lpack

# `luaug test`'s machine-readable report. Written beside the suite when no
# --report path is given, and regenerated on every run.
luaug-test-report.json

# The host writes these beside whatever it was run from (main.cpp): a log file
# and, on a fault, a minidump. They are evidence a person sends, never something
# a repository keeps.
luaug.log
luaug-crash-*.dmp
luaug-crash-*.txt

# `examples/05-streaming`'s world is GENERATED (M7 brief, Decision 8): its
# chunk sources come from `tools/generate_world.luau` and its compiled payloads
# from `luaug build-assets`. What is committed is the forty-line generator, not
# the megabyte and a half it writes -- the roadmap's own deliverable line asks
# for "no giant binary assets in the repo", and generated JSON is the same thing
# wearing a text extension. `run.bat` regenerates it when it is missing.
examples/05-streaming/content/world/
